# Software Design Document (SDD)
## Project Name: CampusCare - Smart Campus Grievance & Complaint Redressal System

---

## 1. Introduction

### 1.1 Purpose
The purpose of this Software Design Document (SDD) is to provide a comprehensive architectural, structural, and behavioral overview of the **CampusCare** platform. It describes the design decisions, component architectures, database schemas, interfaces, and deployment strategies implemented for the system.

### 1.2 Scope
CampusCare is a centralized web-based complaint management and analytics system designed for higher education institutions. It enables students to report campus issues (Hostel, Academic, Wi-Fi, Infrastructure, Canteen, Transport), track grievance lifecycles in real-time, rate resolutions, and access transparent redressal workflows. It equips campus administrators and departmental staff with automated categorization, priority assignment, SLA monitoring, and analytical reporting.

### 1.3 Target Audience
- **College Examiners & Evaluators**: For project assessment, viva evaluation, and architectural review.
- **System Developers & Maintainers**: For codebase maintenance, enhancements, and API integration.
- **Campus Administrators**: For understanding security protocols, role hierarchies, and escalation workflows.

---

## 2. System Architecture

CampusCare follows a clean **Client-Server (3-Tier)** architecture with RESTful communication:

```
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                        PRESENTATION TIER (Frontend)                     |
|  React 18 + Vite | TailwindCSS / Vanilla CSS | Lucide Icons | Chart.js  |
|  - Student Portal: Dashboard, New Ticket, Track Status, Star Rating     |
|  - Staff Portal: Task Queue, Priority Updates, Resolution Notes         |
|  - Admin Portal: Department Overview, Staff Assignment, Analytics Export|
+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+
                                     |
                                     | HTTPS / JSON (REST API)
                                     v
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                        APPLICATION TIER (Backend API)                   |
|  Node.js + Express.js Engine                                            |
|  - Auth Middleware: JWT Token Verification & RBAC                       |
|  - Complaint Engine: Smart Triage, Status State Machine, SLA Counter    |
|  - Analytics Service: Departmental Breakdown, Resolution Rates, Export  |
+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+
                                     |
                                     | CRUD & Index Queries
                                     v
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                           DATA TIER (Storage)                           |
|  JSON Database / MongoDB Atlas Document Store                           |
|  - Collections: Users, Complaints, Departments, Audit Logs              |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

---

## 3. Core Modules & Functionalities

### 3.1 Student Portal Module
- **Authentication**: Email/Student ID login with password hashing.
- **Complaint Submission**: Multi-category selection with file attachments, severity level, location tags, and description.
- **My Tickets View**: Filtered complaint listing isolated to the authenticated student (`/complaints/my`).
- **Campus Complaints Hub**: Read-only public transparency feed of all campus tickets (`/complaints`).
- **Feedback & Ratings**: 1-5 star satisfaction rating and remarks submission upon ticket closure.

### 3.2 Staff Redressal Module
- **Assigned Work Queue**: Filtered list of tickets assigned to the logged-in staff member's department.
- **Status Lifecycle Transitions**: Step-by-step state machine updates (`Submitted` → `Under Review` → `In Progress` → `Resolved` → `Closed`).
- **Resolution Proofs**: Attachment uploads and detailed resolution notes submitted to students.

### 3.3 Admin & Governance Module
- **System Dashboard**: Live KPI cards (Total Tickets, In Progress, Resolved Rate, Escalations).
- **Staff Workload Allocation**: Reassign tickets between staff members with automatic department sync.
- **Export Analytics**: 1-click export of system audit records and performance reports in `.xlsx` and `.pdf` formats.
- **Role-Based Clearance**: Guarded routes preventing unauthorized privilege escalations.

---

## 4. Complaint State Machine

```
[ Submitted ]
      │
      ▼ (Staff Acknowledged)
[ Under Review ]
      │
      ▼ (Assigned to Technician)
[ In Progress ]
      │
      ▼ (Resolution Note + Evidence Provided)
[ Resolved ]
      │
      ▼ (Student Verified / Auto-Closed)
[ Closed ] ──> (Student Satisfaction Rating 1-5 ★)
```

---

## 5. Data Schema & Dictionary

### 5.1 User Entity (`User`)
| Field | Type | Description | Example |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `id` | `String` (PK) | Unique User ID | `usr_student_1` |
| `name` | `String` | Full Name | `"Priya Sharma"` |
| `email` | `String` (Unique) | College Email | `"priya.sharma@college.edu"` |
| `role` | `Enum` | Authorization Level | `"student" \| "staff" \| "admin"` |
| `department` | `String` | Department Tag | `"Computer Science"` |
| `studentId` | `String` | University Roll ID | `"STU-2024-8841"` |

### 5.2 Complaint Entity (`Complaint`)
| Field | Type | Description | Example |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `id` | `String` (PK) | Unique Complaint ID | `cmp_1001` |
| `title` | `String` | Complaint Heading | `"Wi-Fi Disconnection in Lab 3"` |
| `category` | `Enum` | Issue Category | `"Wi-Fi" \| "Hostel" \| "Lab" \| ...` |
| `priority` | `Enum` | Urgency Level | `"Low" \| "Medium" \| "High" \| "Critical"` |
| `status` | `Enum` | Current State | `"Submitted" \| "In Progress" \| "Resolved"` |
| `studentId` | `String` (FK) | Submitting User ID | `usr_student_1` |
| `assignedTo` | `String` (FK) | Assigned Staff ID | `usr_staff_2` |
| `createdAt` | `DateTime` | Timestamp of Filing | `2026-09-20T10:15:00Z` |
| `rating` | `Number` | Student Feedback | `5` |

---

## 6. REST API Specifications

| Method | Endpoint | Access | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/auth/login` | Public | Authenticate user & return JWT token |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/auth/me` | Authenticated | Retrieve current session profile |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/complaints` | Authenticated | List campus complaints (Supports search & filter) |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/complaints/my` | Student | List tickets submitted by current student |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/complaints` | Student | Create new grievance record |
| `PATCH` | `/api/v1/complaints/:id` | Staff / Admin | Update ticket status, priority, or staff |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/complaints/:id/rate` | Student | Submit 1-5 star resolution rating |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/analytics/stats` | Admin | Get summary metrics and department counters |

---

## 7. Security & Non-Functional Requirements

1. **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)**: Enforced both on the client via React Router guards and on the backend via Express middleware.
2. **Data Integrity**: Input validation on complaint payloads; strict validation preventing resolution without explanatory notes.
3. **Responsive UI**: Optimized for mobile phones (375px+), tablets, and widescreen desktop monitors (1920px+).
4. **Offline Resilience**: Local JSON database fallback allowing instant local demonstrations without external network dependency.

---

## 8. Deployment & Execution Summary

- **1-Click Local Execution**: Run `start_campuscare.bat` on Windows to launch backend, frontend, and open browser automatically.
- **Production Cloud Options**:
  - **Frontend**: Deployable on Netlify / Vercel (`dist/` folder, SPA redirect configured via `netlify.toml` / `vercel.json`).
  - **Backend**: Deployable on Render / Railway using `render.yaml` and Node.js runtime.
- **Direct Live Tunnel**: Active localtunnel support (`npx localtunnel --port 5173`) for mobile testing without cloud registration.
